.TH tty "" "Command"
.SH NAME
tty \- print the user's terminal name
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtty\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
tty -- print the user's terminal name
Usage:	tty
.HE
.B tty
prints the pathname of the character-special file associated with
the standard error, which is ordinarily your controlling terminal.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B tty
prints the message `Not a tty' if the standard error is not
associated with a terminal.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B who
